Delete a range spanning a buffer block boundary. The input is larger than
Maxblock (8 KB), so sam splits it across disk blocks; deleting #1,#8990 crosses
the boundary, exercising the multi-block bufdelete path, and the oversized
buffer also drives the block teardown in bufreset at exit.
args: -d input

-- stdin --
#1,#8990d
,p
q
-- stdout --
acccccccccccc
-- stderr --
 -. input
?changed files
-- input --



